# OpenCode iOS port patch -- 0016
# Title: use the real OpenTUI TUI on iPhoneOS when node:ffi is available
# Upstream: anomalyco/opencode @ e8238bae9b807b72ecfc75afd3a9fe2e6b07b944 (v2.2.5)
# Files: packages/cli/src/util/ios.ts, packages/cli/src/commands/handlers/default.ts,
#        packages/cli/src/commands/handlers/mini.ts, packages/cli/vite.node.config.ts
# Depends on: 0011 (iOS TUI guidance) and 0012 (iOS line REPL), which introduced the
#             unconditional iOS fallback branch this patch makes conditional.
# Why: patches 0011/0012 route every iOS build to the line REPL / guidance path as soon as
#      `isIOS()` is true, because the Node 22 iPhoneOS runtime has no node:ffi. Phase D adds an
#      FFI-enabled Node 26.13 iPhoneOS runtime and ships OpenTUI's iPhoneOS renderer as a CLI
#      asset, so on that runtime the real TUI must be attempted instead. The handlers now probe
#      node:ffi lazily (`hasNodeFFI()`: createRequire from node:module, guarded try/catch, so no
#      bundler may try to resolve node:ffi at build time and the Node 22 bundle keeps working):
#        - node:ffi available (FFI-enabled Node 26 + iOS): `opencode` / `opencode mini` fall
#          through to the real OpenTUI TUI path (renderer resolved by the patched
#          @opentui/core resolver from OTUI_ASSET_ROOT -> @opentui/core-ios-arm64/libopentui.dylib);
#        - node:ffi unavailable (Node 22 runtime or a no-FFI Node 26 build): unchanged fallback
#          (line REPL in a TTY, actionable guidance for non-TTY).
#      `isTUIRendererUnavailable` also recognizes the renderer-asset errors ("Missing OpenTUI
#      asset", "OpenTUI native library does not exist") so a partial install degrades to the
#      guidance instead of an OpenTUI stack trace.
#      `IOS_TUI_FFI_GATE` is a marker string kept in the bundle for the node26 build's static
#      gate (scripts/build-opencode-bundle.sh assetcheck greps for it together with hasNodeFFI,
#      runIOSRepl and node:ffi).
# Test: node26 bundle host smoke (--version/--help/debug paths/models/auth list/session list on
#       stock Node 26.13.0 + 24.22.2); bundle static gate; device TUI run with the FFI-enabled
#       runtime (Lead-executed).
# Status: static/host verification only; the real TUI on the device is verified separately.

